"""Engineering blueprints and where their ingredients are found, imported from EDEngineer.

AUTO-GENERATED - do not hand-edit. Regenerate by re-importing:
  https://github.com/msarilar/EDEngineer/blob/master/EDEngineer/Resources/Data/blueprints.json
  https://github.com/msarilar/EDEngineer/blob/master/EDEngineer/Resources/Data/entryData.json
EDEngineer is MIT licensed (notice in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md). Imported 2026-10-13; the project is archived and its data was last changed
2024-03-07, so blueprints and materials added to the game since may be missing. Trimmed to the fields WNTB uses, and the sorted order is WNTB's.

Edited 2026-10-15 to match ED-DDT, which applied data from EDDiscovery's EliteDangerousCore (Apache-2.0; notice in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md;
`tests/test_blueprints.py` pins each change). Re-importing EDEngineer's files would undo them, so reapply them if you do:
- Five synthesis recipes whose ingredients differ now take EDDiscovery's figures: AX Remote Flak Munitions +10% (Weapon Parts for Wreckage
  Components), Chaff Launcher 100% Refill +2 Seconds (Thermic Alloys 1), Flechette Launcher Munitions +10% (Electrochemical Arrays 5,
  Mechanical Components 9), Guardian Gauss Cannon Munitions None (Guardian Power Conduit 2), Guardian Plasma Charger Munitions +30%
  (Phase Alloys 6, Guardian Power Cell 4). Where the two sources disagree EDDiscovery, the more recently maintained, wins; neither is
  Frontier's own list, so a figure may still be wrong.
- Seven synthesis rows EDEngineer lacks: Caustic Sinks, Configurable Small Calibre Munitions (2 grades), Mining Rig, Nanite Munitions, Seismic
  Charge Munitions, Sub-Surface Displacement Munitions; and four ingredient rows for the Thargoid-war materials they use.
- Three "Higher Accuracy (Kinetic, Plasma, Thermal Weapons)" weapon rows removed: duplicates of the "Improved Hip Fire Accuracy" rows.
- The suit and weapon **upgrade** rows (type Suit or Weapon, named for the item, engineer Merchant, grades 2 to 5) now hold the costs the game charges today,
  taken from 17 `UpgradeSuit` / `UpgradeWeapon` events in real journals (2025-2026; EDEngineer's older rows asked for 1, 5, 10 and 15 of each): the schematic,
  the family item and Manufacturing Instructions (or Health Monitor for a suit) take 1, 2, 4 and 5 for classes 2 to 5, and the item's two other materials take
  2, 5, 9 and 12. A suit no longer needs a Power Regulator. Seen for the Karma AR-50, C-44 and L-6, the Manticore Tormentor and Executioner, and the Maverick,
  Artemis and Dominator suits, across classes 2 to 5; the counts were the same for every item and kind, so they are applied to the rest (Karma P-15, Manticore
  Intimidator and Oppressor, the three TK lasers), whose own materials are EDEngineer's. "Manticore Opressor" (EDEngineer's spelling) is "Manticore Oppressor".
- The four Colonia on-foot engineers (Baltanos, Eleanor Bresa, Rosa Dayette, Yi Shen) added to the suit and weapon rows they offer, from
  EDCoPilot's engineer list as ED-DDT applied it (31 rows). Other sources may disagree about which upgrade each offers; this follows ED-DDT.
"""

